---Specifies the status and settings of the GCM channel for an application. This channel enables Amazon Pinpoint to send push notifications through the Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM), formerly Google Cloud Messaging (GCM), service.
---@class aws.pinpoint.GCMChannelRequest
---@field ApiKey? aws.pinpoint.__string The Web API Key, also referred to as an API_KEY or server key, that you received from Google to communicate with Google services.
---@field DefaultAuthenticationMethod? aws.pinpoint.__string The default authentication method used for GCM. Values are either "TOKEN" or "KEY". Defaults to "KEY".
---@field Enabled? aws.pinpoint.__boolean Specifies whether to enable the GCM channel for the application.
---@field ServiceJson? aws.pinpoint.__string The contents of the JSON file provided by Google during registration in order to generate an access token for authentication. For more information see Migrate from legacy FCM APIs to HTTP v1.

---Provides information about the status and settings of the GCM channel for an application. The GCM channel enables Amazon Pinpoint to send push notifications through the Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM), formerly Google Cloud Messaging (GCM), service.
---@class aws.pinpoint.GCMChannelResponse
---@field ApplicationId? aws.pinpoint.__string The unique identifier for the application that the GCM channel applies to.
---@field CreationDate? aws.pinpoint.__string The date and time when the GCM channel was enabled.
---@field Credential? aws.pinpoint.__string The Web API Key, also referred to as an API_KEY or server key, that you received from Google to communicate with Google services.
---@field DefaultAuthenticationMethod? aws.pinpoint.__string The default authentication method used for GCM. Values are either "TOKEN" or "KEY". Defaults to "KEY".
---@field Enabled? aws.pinpoint.__boolean Specifies whether the GCM channel is enabled for the application.
---@field HasCredential? aws.pinpoint.__boolean (Not used) This property is retained only for backward compatibility.
---@field HasFcmServiceCredentials? aws.pinpoint.__boolean Returns true if the JSON file provided by Google during registration process was used in the ServiceJson field of the request.
---@field Id? aws.pinpoint.__string (Deprecated) An identifier for the GCM channel. This property is retained only for backward compatibility.
---@field IsArchived? aws.pinpoint.__boolean Specifies whether the GCM channel is archived.
---@field LastModifiedBy? aws.pinpoint.__string The user who last modified the GCM channel.
---@field LastModifiedDate? aws.pinpoint.__string The date and time when the GCM channel was last modified.
---@field Platform aws.pinpoint.__string The type of messaging or notification platform for the channel. For the GCM channel, this value is GCM.
---@field Version? aws.pinpoint.__integer The current version of the GCM channel.

---Specifies the settings for a one-time message that's sent directly to an endpoint through the GCM channel. The GCM channel enables Amazon Pinpoint to send messages to the Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM), formerly Google Cloud Messaging (GCM), service.
---@class aws.pinpoint.GCMMessage
---@field Action? aws.pinpoint.Action|string The action to occur if the recipient taps the push notification. Valid values are:
---@field Body? aws.pinpoint.__string The body of the notification message.
---@field CollapseKey? aws.pinpoint.__string An arbitrary string that identifies a group of messages that can be collapsed to ensure that only the last message is sent when delivery can resume. This helps avoid sending too many instances of the same messages when the recipient's device comes online again or becomes active.
---@field Data? aws.pinpoint.MapOf__string The JSON data payload to use for the push notification, if the notification is a silent push notification. This payload is added to the data.pinpoint.jsonBody object of the notification.
---@field IconReference? aws.pinpoint.__string The icon image name of the asset saved in your app.
---@field ImageIconUrl? aws.pinpoint.__string The URL of the large icon image to display in the content view of the push notification.
---@field ImageUrl? aws.pinpoint.__string The URL of an image to display in the push notification.
---@field PreferredAuthenticationMethod? aws.pinpoint.__string The preferred authentication method, with valid values "KEY" or "TOKEN". If a value isn't provided then the DefaultAuthenticationMethod is used.
---@field Priority? aws.pinpoint.__string para>normal – The notification might be delayed. Delivery is optimized for battery usage on the recipient's device. Use this value unless immediate delivery is required.
---@field RawContent? aws.pinpoint.__string The raw, JSON-formatted string to use as the payload for the notification message. If specified, this value overrides all other content for the message.
---@field RestrictedPackageName? aws.pinpoint.__string The package name of the application where registration tokens must match in order for the recipient to receive the message.
---@field SilentPush? aws.pinpoint.__boolean Specifies whether the notification is a silent push notification, which is a push notification that doesn't display on a recipient's device. Silent push notifications can be used for cases such as updating an app's configuration or supporting phone home functionality.
---@field SmallImageIconUrl? aws.pinpoint.__string The URL of the small icon image to display in the status bar and the content view of the push notification.
---@field Sound? aws.pinpoint.__string The sound to play when the recipient receives the push notification. You can use the default stream or specify the file name of a sound resource that's bundled in your app. On an Android platform, the sound file must reside in /res/raw/.
---@field Substitutions? aws.pinpoint.MapOfListOf__string The default message variables to use in the notification message. You can override the default variables with individual address variables.
---@field TimeToLive? aws.pinpoint.__integer The amount of time, in seconds, that FCM should store and attempt to deliver the push notification, if the service is unable to deliver the notification the first time. If you don't specify this value, FCM defaults to the maximum value, which is 2,419,200 seconds (28 days).
---@field Title? aws.pinpoint.__string The title to display above the notification message on the recipient's device.
---@field Url? aws.pinpoint.__string The URL to open in the recipient's default mobile browser, if a recipient taps the push notification and the value of the Action property is URL.

