---Specifies the settings for a job that imports endpoint definitions from an Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) bucket.
---@class aws.pinpoint.ImportJobRequest
---@field DefineSegment? aws.pinpoint.__boolean Specifies whether to create a segment that contains the endpoints, when the endpoint definitions are imported.
---@field ExternalId? aws.pinpoint.__string (Deprecated) Your AWS account ID, which you assigned to an external ID key in an IAM trust policy. Amazon Pinpoint previously used this value to assume an IAM role when importing endpoint definitions, but we removed this requirement. We don't recommend use of external IDs for IAM roles that are assumed by Amazon Pinpoint.
---@field Format aws.pinpoint.Format|string The format of the files that contain the endpoint definitions to import. Valid values are: CSV, for comma-separated values format; and, JSON, for newline-delimited JSON format. If the Amazon S3 location stores multiple files that use different formats, Amazon Pinpoint imports data only from the files that use the specified format.
---@field RegisterEndpoints? aws.pinpoint.__boolean Specifies whether to register the endpoints with Amazon Pinpoint, when the endpoint definitions are imported.
---@field RoleArn aws.pinpoint.__string The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) role that authorizes Amazon Pinpoint to access the Amazon S3 location to import endpoint definitions from.
---@field S3Url aws.pinpoint.__string The URL of the Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) bucket that contains the endpoint definitions to import. This location can be a folder or a single file. If the location is a folder, Amazon Pinpoint imports endpoint definitions from the files in this location, including any subfolders that the folder contains.
---@field SegmentId? aws.pinpoint.__string The identifier for the segment to update or add the imported endpoint definitions to, if the import job is meant to update an existing segment.
---@field SegmentName? aws.pinpoint.__string A custom name for the segment that's created by the import job, if the value of the DefineSegment property is true.

---Provides information about the resource settings for a job that imports endpoint definitions from one or more files. The files can be stored in an Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) bucket or uploaded directly from a computer by using the Amazon Pinpoint console.
---@class aws.pinpoint.ImportJobResource
---@field DefineSegment? aws.pinpoint.__boolean Specifies whether the import job creates a segment that contains the endpoints, when the endpoint definitions are imported.
---@field ExternalId? aws.pinpoint.__string (Deprecated) Your AWS account ID, which you assigned to an external ID key in an IAM trust policy. Amazon Pinpoint previously used this value to assume an IAM role when importing endpoint definitions, but we removed this requirement. We don't recommend use of external IDs for IAM roles that are assumed by Amazon Pinpoint.
---@field Format aws.pinpoint.Format The format of the files that contain the endpoint definitions to import. Valid values are: CSV, for comma-separated values format; and, JSON, for newline-delimited JSON format.
---@field RegisterEndpoints? aws.pinpoint.__boolean Specifies whether the import job registers the endpoints with Amazon Pinpoint, when the endpoint definitions are imported.
