---@field CustomDeliveryConfiguration? aws.pinpoint.CustomDeliveryConfiguration The delivery configuration settings for sending the campaign through a custom channel. This object is required if the MessageConfiguration object for the campaign specifies a CustomMessage object.
---@field Description? aws.pinpoint.__string A custom description of the campaign.
---@field HoldoutPercent? aws.pinpoint.__integer The allocated percentage of users (segment members) who shouldn't receive messages from the campaign.
---@field Hook? aws.pinpoint.CampaignHook The settings for the AWS Lambda function to invoke as a code hook for the campaign. You can use this hook to customize the segment that's used by the campaign.
---@field IsPaused? aws.pinpoint.__boolean Specifies whether to pause the campaign. A paused campaign doesn't run unless you resume it by changing this value to false.
---@field Limits? aws.pinpoint.CampaignLimits The messaging limits for the campaign.
---@field MessageConfiguration? aws.pinpoint.MessageConfiguration The message configuration settings for the campaign.
---@field Name? aws.pinpoint.__string A custom name for the campaign.
---@field Schedule? aws.pinpoint.Schedule The schedule settings for the campaign.
---@field SegmentId? aws.pinpoint.__string The unique identifier for the segment to associate with the campaign.
---@field SegmentVersion? aws.pinpoint.__integer The version of the segment to associate with the campaign.
---@field tags? aws.pinpoint.MapOf__string As of 22-05-2023 tags has been deprecated for update operations. After this date any value in tags is not processed and an error code is not returned. To manage tags we recommend using either Tags in the API Reference for Amazon Pinpoint, resourcegroupstaggingapi commands in the AWS Command Line Interface Documentation or resourcegroupstaggingapi in the AWS SDK. (Deprecated) A string-to-string map...
---@field TemplateConfiguration? aws.pinpoint.TemplateConfiguration The message template to use for the campaign.
---@field TreatmentDescription? aws.pinpoint.__string A custom description of the default treatment for the campaign.
---@field TreatmentName? aws.pinpoint.__string A custom name of the default treatment for the campaign, if the campaign has multiple treatments. A treatment is a variation of a campaign that's used for A/B testing.
---@field Priority? aws.pinpoint.__integer Defines the priority of the campaign, used to decide the order of messages displayed to user if there are multiple messages scheduled to be displayed at the same moment.

---Specifies the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of an event stream to publish events to and the AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) role to use when publishing those events.
---@class aws.pinpoint.WriteEventStream
---@field DestinationStreamArn aws.pinpoint.__string The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Amazon Kinesis data stream or Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream that you want to publish event data to.
---@field RoleArn aws.pinpoint.__string The AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) role that authorizes Amazon Pinpoint to publish event data to the stream in your AWS account.

---Specifies the configuration and other settings for a journey.
---@class aws.pinpoint.WriteJourneyRequest
---@field Activities? aws.pinpoint.MapOfActivity A map that contains a set of Activity objects, one object for each activity in the journey. For each Activity object, the key is the unique identifier (string) for an activity and the value is the settings for the activity. An activity identifier can contain a maximum of 100 characters. The characters must be alphanumeric characters.
---@field CreationDate? aws.pinpoint.__string The date, in ISO 8601 format, when the journey was created.
---@field LastModifiedDate? aws.pinpoint.__string The date, in ISO 8601 format, when the journey was last modified.
---@field Limits? aws.pinpoint.JourneyLimits The messaging and entry limits for the journey.
---@field LocalTime? aws.pinpoint.__boolean Specifies whether the journey's scheduled start and end times use each participant's local time. To base the schedule on each participant's local time, set this value to true.
---@field Name aws.pinpoint.__string The name of the journey. A journey name can contain a maximum of 150 characters. The characters can be alphanumeric characters or symbols, such as underscores (_) or hyphens (-). A journey name can't contain any spaces.
---@field QuietTime? aws.pinpoint.QuietTime The quiet time settings for the journey. Quiet time is a specific time range when a journey doesn't send messages to participants, if all the following conditions are met:
---@field RefreshFrequency? aws.pinpoint.__string The frequency with which Amazon Pinpoint evaluates segment and event data for the journey, as a duration in ISO 8601 format.
---@field Schedule? aws.pinpoint.JourneySchedule The schedule settings for the journey.
---@field StartActivity? aws.pinpoint.__string The unique identifier for the first activity in the journey. The identifier for this activity can contain a maximum of 128 characters. The characters must be alphanumeric characters.
---@field StartCondition? aws.pinpoint.StartCondition The segment that defines which users are participants in the journey.
---@field State? aws.pinpoint.State|string The status of the journey. Valid values are:
---@field WaitForQuietTime? aws.pinpoint.__boolean Specifies whether endpoints in quiet hours should enter a wait till the end of their quiet hours.
---@field RefreshOnSegmentUpdate? aws.pinpoint.__boolean Indicates whether the journey participants should be refreshed when a segment is updated.
---@field JourneyChannelSettings? aws.pinpoint.JourneyChannelSettings The channel-specific configurations for the journey.
---@field SendingSchedule? aws.pinpoint.__boolean Indicates if journey has Advance Quiet Time enabled. This flag should be set to true in order to allow using OpenHours and ClosedDays.
---@field OpenHours? aws.pinpoint.OpenHours The time when journey allow to send messages. QuietTime should be configured first and SendingSchedule should be set to true.
---@field ClosedDays? aws.pinpoint.ClosedDays The time when journey will stop sending messages. QuietTime should be configured first and SendingSchedule should be set to true.
---@field TimezoneEstimationMethods? aws.pinpoint.ListOf__TimezoneEstimationMethodsElement An array of time zone estimation methods, if any, to use for determining an Endpoints time zone if the Endpoint does not have a value for the Demographic.Timezone attribute.

---Specifies the configuration, dimension, and other settings for a segment. A WriteSegmentRequest object can include a Dimensions object or a SegmentGroups object, but not both.
---@class aws.pinpoint.WriteSegmentRequest
---@field Dimensions? aws.pinpoint.SegmentDimensions The criteria that define the dimensions for the segment.
---@field Name? aws.pinpoint.__string The name of the segment.
---@field SegmentGroups? aws.pinpoint.SegmentGroupList The segment group to use and the dimensions to apply to the group's base segments in order to build the segment. A segment group can consist of zero or more base segments. Your request can include only one segment group.
